    "chapters": [
      {
        "id": "build-release",
        "title": "How the 0.0.5 version reaches packages, checkpoints, and releases",
        "claims": [
          {
            "text": "setup.py executes version.py in a separate dictionary and passes its __version__ value to setup(version=...). That makes 0.0.5 the package base version; the CUDA wheel build still supplies its CUDA and Torch build tag separately.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_fe815383647e4eef8b58ca30c2ffeaff",
              "call_d4e2a681e431445aa3e1c98f13992e5c",
              "call_9c197a162be24859bbec715e03096325"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "compile_model imports __version__ and writes 0.0.5 as quantization_config.version in the output config.json only when the input has no quantization_config. If the section already exists, the function updates bits and head_bits without replacing or backfilling its version. The companion quantization_config.json takes that resulting section and adds tensor-storage metadata.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_fe815383647e4eef8b58ca30c2ffeaff",
              "call_22472de624414a9ebe994d2264426ed6",
              "call_c5c5a97c093b4fd3b754f79eb6c4bb57"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "The manually dispatched build workflow reads version.py as text. With 0.0.5 captured, it uses v0.0.5 as the release tag and 0.0.5 as the release name. The upload step targets ./dist/*.whl and requires both a successful version parse and release input '1'; that input defaults to '0'.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_fe815383647e4eef8b58ca30c2ffeaff",
              "call_9c197a162be24859bbec715e03096325"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "A standard-library check executed the parent assignment and the new assignment transcribed from the diff, then applied the workflow regex in Python. The assignment and capture agreed for both inputs, yielding 0.0.4 and 0.0.5 and the corresponding v-prefixed tag strings.",
            "basis": "execution",
            "evidence": [
              "call_fe815383647e4eef8b58ca30c2ffeaff",
              "call_9c197a162be24859bbec715e03096325",
              "call_b353eca4bb2c498598a1b7b9fa9aa959"
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "findings": [],
    "summary": "Bumps ExLlamaV3 from 0.0.4 to 0.0.5, updating package metadata, the version stamp for newly created EXL3 quantization configs, and conditional release naming."
